From 12cca5b4557bc42a5730929a3ee7da85e9a85e9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:29:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: scan scripts run behind shell
 reserved words (time, !, if/then, {, coproc)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Inside the supervised gateway `./x.sh` (x.sh = `hermes gateway restart`) was refused, but
`time ./x.sh`, `! ./x.sh`, `if true; then ./x.sh; fi`, `{ ./x.sh; }` and
`while false; do ./x.sh; done` ran. Reproduced on main 8ecf7ef242 through
gateway_lifecycle_block().

Why: the referenced-script walk read each segment at its first non-assignment token and at the
wrapper-peeled one. A leading reserved word is neither, so the walk took `time`/`!`/`then`/`{`/`do`
for the command and never opened the script. The interpreter walk (`time python3 x.py`), the
`sh -c` / `env -S` / `su -c` payload walk (`then bash -c './x.sh'`), the over-budget fail-closed
path (it only applies to discovered scripts) and `launchctl submit` detection had the same gap.
time(1) as a program (`/usr/bin/time ./x.sh`, `command time ./x.sh`) was not a wrapper either.

Fix (additive; no reference is ever removed):
- `_command_segment_views()` yields each segment as written and, when it starts with reserved
  words, without them (`_peel_command_keywords`, from executes_command_named). The shell-script,
  interpreter and payload walks and contains_launchctl_submit_command read every view, then
  peel env assignments and wrappers as before.
- `_COMMAND_PREFIX_KEYWORDS` gains `coproc` (and `coproc NAME { … }` skips NAME).
- `time` joins the transparent wrappers, with `-f/--format/-o/--output` taking a value.

Tests: tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_reserved_words.py — 51 killing cases (shell scripts,
sourced scripts, interpreter runs, sh -c payloads, launchctl submit, over-budget fail-closed)
plus mention/additivity guards; test_hint_survives_reserved_words now goes through the full
_refuse path, and executes_command_named covers coproc and time(1).
RED on f56d54960f (base): 62 failed. GREEN: 96 passed; tests/cron + approval/terminal/code
execution suites 2903 passed, 4 skipped; scripts/check ok.

Card: t_01a1d4cd34067afe
